 "customerTurns": 5,
 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "bosch 24 not draining, water sitting in bottom. help"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Water sitting in the bottom usually means the drain pump can't push it out. The most common cause is a blockage in the filter area or something (like glass or a bone) stuck in the pump itself. Please switch off and unplug the dishwasher first for safety. Then twist and lift out the round filter at the bottom of the tub, and look into the sump underneath. Is it blocked with food/debris, or can you see anything stuck in the small plastic impeller blades there?\n[Helpful to see: image \"Where the filter is\" — The filter sits in the base of the dishwasher, usually under the bottom spray arm. Twist it out anticlockwise and rinse it under a tap. Typical layout — your dishwasher may differ.]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "filter's clogged with food and a bit of broken glass. never cleaned it. display says E:24"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That explains it perfectly: E:24 is Bosch's code for a drainage fault caused by a blockage. Please switch off and unplug the dishwasher again. Use a sponge or cup to bail out the standing water from the base of the tub so it's dry enough to see clearly. Look into the sump (the area where the filter was) for any remaining glass shards or food, and remove them carefully. There is usually a small plastic cover in the very centre of the sump; lift its clip to reveal the drain pump impeller blades underneath. Check if they turn freely by hand or if they are jammed/broken by the glass."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "cover clips in fine, impeller turns. there's broken glass in there, do I need gloves?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, please wear sturdy gloves to protect your hands from the broken glass. Carefully remove all visible shards and food debris from the sump area and the filter housing. Once it is completely clear, put the filter back in place securely."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok cleared it, filter back in. what now, run a cycle?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, please go ahead and run a cycle. I recommend starting with a rinse or drain programme first to confirm the water clears properly before running a full wash. To help prevent this from happening again in future, try to scrape large food scraps off your plates into the bin before loading them. Let me know if the error returns."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ran a rinse. drains normally, E:24 gone"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That is excellent news. To help prevent this from happening again in future, try to scrape large food scraps off your plates into the bin before loading them. Let me know if there is anything else I can help you with."
  }
 ],
